OL,3,AOrange Order to appeal High Court
OL,4,Ainjunction stopping Drumcree parade
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Orange Order has lodged an appeal
OL,7,Fagainst a High Court ruling banning
OL,8,FPortadown Orangemen from marching along
OL,9,Fthe mainly nationalist Garvaghy Road on
OL,10,FSunday.
OL,12,FOn Friday the Parades Commission
OL,13,Fannounced that the Orange Order parade
OL,14,Fcould proceed for the first time in
OL,15,Falmost 30 years with restrictions in
OL,16,Fplace.
OL,18,FThe Garvaghy Road Residents' Coalition
OL,19,F(GRRC) had mounted a legal challenge to
OL,20,Fthe decision and a High Court judge on
OL,21,FSaturday afternoon issued an injunction
OL,22,Ftemporarily halting the march.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,308,300,200,140,0,100
